Hmm, but wait — "deliberate and tested" per the repo's own degradation doctrine... The test comment says "no allowlist to match against — cannot call the actor a machine". The counter-argument: the AC5 docblock says "missing proof refuses (fail closed)" — but missing ALLOWLIST is different from missing proof. Since smGuestTransplant config is required to arm the rule at all, and a deployment configuring smGuestTransplant would almost surely have machineAuthor configured (it's a global factory knob)... I'll go IMPORTANT with a question flavor. Actually, per the severity rules: "IMPORTANT — real maintainability or correctness issue. Strongly prefer fixing before merge." This qualifies as a security-hardening question → IMPORTANT.

Now the sweep complete_orphan dead-branch issue. Let me trace it once more carefully to be sure — this is my strongest finding candidate.

