   return { decision: 'skip', reason: 'same-repo', ... };
}
``

`isCrossRepoHead(null, owner, repo)` → `typeof null !== 'string'` → returns false → skip. 

CONFIRMED: sweep's complete_orphan ALWAYS produces decision 'skip — same-repo'. The orphan branch with an armed marker is never completed by the sweep. The audit log is misleading ('completing orphan transplant on ... (E5)' immediately followed by 'skipped — same-repo head').

Also `machineLogins = []` passed → classifyArmActor → 'human' (works by the empty-allowlist behavior — ironically the fail-open helps here).

And ALSO: the armed-marker orphan completion in the sweep re-enters `transplantGuestPrAction`, which calls `resolveHeadSha(repoInfo, ticket)` — github_get_pr on the source PR — plus `guestMarker`, `guestArmEvent`, `guestBranchExists`, `guestOpenPrOnBranch` — all live probes. So even if headRepo were set, the re-entry does the full probe set. The skip makes all that wasted work, plus the E5 orphan-completion promise in the GC sweep is unfulfilled — the main action path still completes orphans when the source PR surfaces in the query (it has the real headRepo), so the system eventually converges IF the source PR still matches the rule query (it must have po_accept label and not be blocked...). Actually wait — will the source PR surface? The rule query: labels=[po_accept], notLabels=[agent:rework], notMachine, crossRepo, draft:false, allowBlockedItems. An orphan from a dead tick: the source PR still has po_accept (the marker comment 'armed' was posted, the branch was cut, tick died before merge). Next tick: query matches (po_accept present, open, cross-repo) → main path: _orphanDecision → marker armed + no open PR → complete-orphan → works (real headRepo). So E5 converges via the main path; the sweep's complete_orphan is a redundant dead branch. Severity: IMPORTANT (dead wiring branch + misleading log; convergence still happens through the other path — but only while the source PR remains open+labeled; if the source PR got closed by a human meanwhile, the sweep's completion would have been the only path, and it never works).

